    file_path: the path of this file, args: {'file_path': {'title': 'File Path', 'type': 'string'}}
file_write_tool: Write content into a file at the specified path.

Args:
    content: The content to write into the file.
    file_path: The full path of the file to be written., args: {'content': {'title': 'Content', 'type': 'string'}, 'file_path': {'title': 'File Path', 'type': 'string'}}
image_build_tool: Build a Docker image from a specific Dockerfile.

Args:
    docker_file_path (str): Path to the Dockerfile (relative to build context)
    image_tag (str): Tag name for the resulting image, args: {'docker_file_path': {'title': 'Docker File Path', 'type': 'string'}, 'image_tag': {'title': 'Image Tag', 'type': 'string'}}
container_run_tool: start and run a Docker container from a specified image.

Args:
    image_tag: The tag of the image to run the container from.
    container_name: The name to assign to the new container.
    internal_port: Port used inside the container.
    expose_port: The host port to map to the container's internal port., args: {'image_tag': {'title': 'Image Tag', 'type': 'string'}, 'container_name': {'title': 'Container Name', 'type': 'string'}, 'internal_port': {'title': 'Internal Port', 'type': 'integer'}, 'expose_port': {'title': 'Expose Port', 'type': 'integer'}}
container_exec_cmd_tool: Execute a shell command inside an already running Docker container.
The command is run with `sh -c`, so cd, && and pipes work.

Args:
    container_name: The name of the container.
    command: The command to execute, args: {'container_name': {'title': 'Container Name', 'type': 'string'}, 'command': {'title': 'Command', 'type': 'string'}}
failure_diagnosis_tool: identify the failure reason and suggest a solution

Args:
    failure_msg: details about current failure, args: {'failure_msg': {'title': 'Failure Msg', 'type': 'string'}}
container_logs_tool: Show the latest log lines of a container to check whether the application inside
started correctly. Use it after container_run_tool, before giving the final answer.

Args:
    container_name: The name of the container.
    wait_seconds: Seconds to wait before reading the logs (gives the app time to start, max 120).
    tail: Number of last log lines to return., args: {'container_name': {'title': 'Container Name', 'type': 'string'}, 'wait_seconds': {'default': 20, 'title': 'Wait Seconds', 'type': 'integer'}, 'tail': {'default': 40, 'title': 'Tail', 'type': 'integer'}}
container_remove_tool: Stop and remove ONE container created for this task (for example an old or broken one
with the same name) so it can be re-created. Kubernetes/kind system containers are refused.

Args:
    container_name: The name of the container to remove., args: {'container_name': {'title': 'Container Name', 'type': 'string'}}
k8s_manifest_generate_tool: Generate Kubernetes Deployment + Service YAML for an application with the LLM,
check it (allowed kinds and namespace) and save it to a file.

Args:
    app_name: Name for the Deployment, the Service and the app label.
    image: Container image, e.g. vue-paper-dashboard:latest (local images are allowed).
    container_port: Port the application listens on inside the container.
    replicas: Number of Pod replicas.
    namespace: Target namespace (must start with lab3-).
    service_port: Port exposed by the ClusterIP Service.
    save_path: Where to save the YAML, e.g. k8s/vue-paper-dashboard.yaml, args: {'app_name': {'title': 'App Name', 'type': 'string'}, 'image': {'title': 'Image', 'type': 'string'}, 'container_port': {'title': 'Container Port', 'type': 'integer'}, 'replicas': {'title': 'Replicas', 'type': 'integer'}, 'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}, 'service_port': {'title': 'Service Port', 'type': 'integer'}, 'save_path': {'title': 'Save Path', 'type': 'string'}}
k8s_namespace_tool: Create a Kubernetes namespace if it does not exist yet.
Only namespaces starting with lab3- are allowed.

Args:
    namespace: Name of the namespace., args: {'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}}
k8s_apply_tool: Check a YAML manifest (allowed kinds, namespace, server-side dry run) and apply it with kubectl.

Args:
    manifest_path: Path of the YAML file.
    namespace: Target namespace (must start with lab3-)., args: {'manifest_path': {'title': 'Manifest Path', 'type': 'string'}, 'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}}
k8s_wait_ready_tool: Wait until all Pods of a Deployment are Ready (kubectl rollout status), then list the Pods.

Args:
    namespace: Namespace of the Deployment.
    deployment: Name of the Deployment.
    timeout_seconds: Maximum time to wait (30-900 seconds)., args: {'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}, 'deployment': {'title': 'Deployment', 'type': 'string'}, 'timeout_seconds': {'default': 300, 'title': 'Timeout Seconds', 'type': 'integer'}}
k8s_pod_logs_tool: Show recent logs of a Deployment's Pods and the latest namespace events,
to find out why Pods are not Ready or why the application fails.

Args:
    namespace: Namespace of the Deployment.
    deployment: Name of the Deployment.
    tail: Number of log lines to return., args: {'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}, 'deployment': {'title': 'Deployment', 'type': 'string'}, 'tail': {'default': 40, 'title': 'Tail', 'type': 'integer'}}
k8s_service_check_tool: Check that a Service really answers HTTP: show the Service and its endpoints, open a temporary
kubectl port-forward and send an HTTP GET request through it.

